distinguishing normal versus abnormal chest radiographs and generalization to two unseen diseases tuberculosis and COVID-19. Sci Rep. 2021 Dec 1;11(1) doi: 10.1038/s41598-021-93967-2. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 11. Heiliger L, Sekuboyina A, Menze B, Egger J, Kleesiek J. Beyond Medical Imaging: A Review of Multimodal Deep Learning in Radiology 12. Pham HH, Le TT, Tran DQ, Ngo DT, Nguyen HQ. Interpreting chest X-rays via CNNs that exploit hierarchical disease dependencies and uncertainty labels. 2019 Nov 14. Available from: http://arxiv.org/abs/1911.06475 . 13. Yuan Z, Yan Y, Sonka M, Yang T. Large-scale Robust Deep AUC Maximization: A New Surrogate Loss and Empirical Studies on Medical Image Classification. 2020 Dec 5. Available from: http://arxiv.org/abs/2012.03173 . 14. Karimi D, Dou H, Warfield SK, Gholipour A. Deep learning with noisy labels: Exploring techniques and remedies in medical image analysis. Med Image Anal. 2020 Oct;65:101759. doi: 10.1016/j.media.2020.101759. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Eyre H, Chapman AB, Peterson KS, Shi J, Alba PR, Jones MM, et al. Launching into clinical space with medspaCy: a new clinical text processing toolkit in Python. 2021 Jun 14. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 16. Huang G, Liu Z, van der Maaten L, Weinberger KQ. Densely Connected Convolutional Networks. 2016 Aug 24. 17. Kingma DP, Ba J. Adam: A Method for Stochastic Optimization. 2014 Dec 22. 18. Lin TY, Goyal P, Girshick R, He K, Dollár P. Focal Loss for Dense Object Detection. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 19. Li Y, Yang J, Song Y, Cao L, Luo J, Li LJ. Learning from Noisy Labels with Distillation. 2017 Mar 7. Available from: http://arxiv.org/abs/1703.02391 . 20. Selvaraju RR, Cogswell M, Das A, Vedantam R, Parikh D, Batra D. 2017 IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV) IEEE; 2017. Grad-CAM: Visual Explanations from Deep Networks via Gradient-Based Localization; pp. p. 618–26. [ Google Scholar ] 21. G